  "result": "The gate returned `WITNESS_FAIL` on the first of six runs. I stopped there because the cause is in the run's reading, not in the rule. Only the `forbid` scene failed: the electric scooter's verdict came out unknown instead of violated, with the reason `aggregate_unresolved:DEF-LVMC-11-02-083::electric_scooter`. No other scene was reported failing.\n\n**Why it fails.** In the run's reading, the `DEF-LVMC-11-02-083::electric_scooter` group includes no road-user class, and lists `ru.electric_scooter` itself as unresolved. Under the `ru.aggregate` contract that means no road user can ever be confirmed as a member. So the rule can never find an electric scooter on the Fremont Street sidewalk in violation, even though the law names electric scooters outright.\n\n**What should change.** The reading should list `ru.electric_scooter` as included under `DEF-LVMC-11-02-083::electric_scooter`, since the definition (\"a device with handlebars and an electric motor\") describes that class. Alternatively, the plan could map \"electric scooter\" to the class atom `ru.electric_scooter`. Either way, the rule file itself needs no change.\n\nI did not replace the scooter in `forbid` with an electric bicycle. That would have passed the gate, but the scene would no longer match the planned narrative and the problem would be hidden.\n\n**What I wrote:**\n- **Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_180_A.lean`):\n  - **Class:** the subject belongs to one of the three groups the node names (bicycle, electric bicycle, electric scooter).\n  - **Applies when:** the subject is on some sidewalk region, and the place is declared to be Fremont Street between Main and Seventh.\n  - **Duty:** the subject is at rest, using `drv_motion_complete_halt` with `p.halt_speed_tolerance`.\n  - **Narrowings:** none; the record left no reading open.\n- **Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_180_A.lean`): a sidewalk alongside a roadway, with each device's body entirely inside one of them. Moving devices travel at 3 m/s (the tolerance is 0.1 m/s). In `permit` the bicycle's speed is 0, `blind` hides the speed, and `branch_1` declares the place outside the named stretch.\n- **Report:** `task_result.md` in the working directory has the gate run, the choices, and this explanation.",
